{%- comment -%}
  journal-assets
  ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Loads the fonts + CSS/JS this feature needs, without requiring any
  edit to layout/theme.liquid. Rendered once from journal-hero.liquid
  and article-hero.liquid — the guaranteed-first section on the two
  JOURNAL templates — so it's present on every JOURNAL page exactly
  once per request.

  By default this loads everything (fonts + theme.css + theme.js +
  journal.css + journal.js), so JOURNAL renders correctly even on a
  theme that doesn't already have this design system (e.g. stock
  Dawn on a test store). Make sure all 4 files below are uploaded to
  Assets, or the affected styling/behaviour will be missing.

  ONLY IF you're installing this into the real production theme that
  ALREADY has the matching site-wide design (same --black/--gold
  tokens, same .site-header/.reveal/.nav-toggle behaviour already
  loaded by its own theme.liquid) should you comment out the
  theme.css/theme.js lines below — loading them a second time there
  would double up JS event listeners (e.g. the hamburger menu opening
  and immediately re-closing). journal.css/journal.js are always
  needed either way; they're genuinely new.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400&family=Noto+Sans+JP:wght@300;400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'theme.css' | asset_url }}">
<script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'journal.css' | asset_url }}">
<script src="{{ 'journal.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
